  "estimatedMinutes": 2,
  "statement": "In trapezoid \\(ABCD,\\) sides \\(AB\\) and \\(CD\\) are parallel, and diagonal \\(BD\\) and side \\(AD\\) have equal length. If \\(\\angle DCB=110^\\circ\\) and \\(\\angle CBD=30^\\circ,\\) then \\(\\angle ADB=\\)",
  "answerChoices": [
    {
      "label": "A",
      "text": "\\(80^\\circ\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "B",
      "text": "\\(90^\\circ\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "C",
      "text": "\\(100^\\circ\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "text": "\\(110^\\circ\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "E",
      "text": "\\(120^\\circ\\)"
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "c",
    "value": "100"
